# Question 1
- Read `"data/gene_categories.csv"` and create a pie chart showing the number of genes in each functional category. Add:
* Percentage labels for each slice (e.g., "DNA Repair: 22.5%")
* A title **"Distribution of Gene Numbers by Functional Category"**
* Use distinct colors for each category
    
    <span style="color:#8b0153;">Hint</span>: Use `value_counts()` on the `functional_category` column to count genes in each category, then `plt.pie()` with `autopct='%1.1f%%'`
<br></br>

# Question 2
- Using the same dataset, create a bar chart showing the number of genes in each functional category. Then:
* Add x-label **"Functional Category"**, y-label **"Number of Genes"**
* Rotate x-axis labels 45 degrees for better readability
* Add a grid with dashed lines
    
    <span style="color:#8b0153;">Hint</span>: Use `plt.bar()` with category names and their counts
<br></br>

# Question 3
- Create a line graph showing expression levels of a `'TP53'` across different time points (0h, 2h, 4h, 8h, 12h, 24h). Then:
* Add markers at each data point
* Make the line green and dashed
* Add appropriate labels and title
    
    <span style="color:#8b0153;">Hint</span>: Use `plt.plot()` with `marker='o'` and `linestyle='--'`

<br></br>
</div>